    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d819">

                <pb facs="1040" n="926" xml:id="pg926"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2531/32</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-09-30">September 30, 1931</date>.<lb/>[Received October
                        10.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 976</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my telegram No. 119, September
                    25, 6 p.m., I have the honor to transmit copies of the notes exchanged on
                    September 28 with the Chilean Government on commercial policy (Enclosures Nos. 1
                    and 2).<anchor n="8" xml:id="d819-f1"/></p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>After the elections I hope that conditions will be such with the new Government
                    that negotiations for a definite commercial treaty may soon be resumed and I
                    would appreciate appropriate instructions.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. S. Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
